cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite the paper below."
title: "ZeroLINC: Training-Free Local Classification of Security Incident Reports"
abstract: >-
  An open-source command-line tool that assigns SOC/CSIRT incident tickets to the 12
  categories derived from NIST SP 800-61r3, locally and with no model training and no
  external API. It carries two engines: an instance-memory engine that votes over
  previously labeled tickets, and a zero-shot engine for deployments with no labeled data.
